  "slug": "coding-rnas-generates-6c5b",
  "summary": "Four multimodal atlases now align human, macaque, marmoset, and mouse basal ganglia cell taxonomies within shared ontologies and spatial reference frames.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is cross-species harmonization of basal ganglia cell taxonomies. A multiomic atlas of 1.8 million primate basal ganglia nuclei identifies 61 conserved cell types and maps disease risk to populations. A companion spatial transcriptomics study profiles over one million cells per species in human, macaque, and marmoset, integrated with snRNA-seq. A BICAN multimodal atlas spanning human, macaque, marmoset, and mouse integrates single-cell transcriptomics. What is new across these reports is the pairing of a shared ontology with spatial reference frames: HOMBA provides a harmonized ontology and 3D reference atlases for human, macaque, and marmoset basal ganglia onto which cellular taxonomies are mapped.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-19"
}
